## O1 — closed default list

```
F.6 COSMETIC DEFAULTS — CLOSED LIST

    A default may be applied ONLY if all three hold:
      (a) the field appears in the table below
      (b) no input.conform entry could govern it
      (c) the user stated nothing bearing on it

    field                  default
    ---------------------  ----------------------------------------
    heading_style          sentence case, unnumbered
    date_format            ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD)
    enumeration_marker     arabic for ordered, hyphen for unordered
    citation_style         inline parenthetical
    absence_notation       none / none stated / none supplied

    THE LIST IS CLOSED. Do not apply a default by analogy to a listed
    one. Any cosmetic gap not on this list is [UNSPECIFIED].

    If input.conform is populated, suppress ALL defaults in this table.
    The schema is the authority and you cannot read it. Record
    `defaults_applied: suppressed (conform present)`.

    Never default: voice, tone, register, length, structure, ordering,
    format of the deliverable itself. These are downstream property or
    material gaps.
```

The suppression clause is the load-bearing part — without it Goal silently overrides a schema it has never seen.

---

## O2 — acceptance gate

```
F.7 ACCEPTED WHEN — VALIDATION GATE

    Every candidate acceptance condition passes BOTH tests or it does
    not enter this slot.

    BINARY:     admits exactly one of pass / fail on inspection.
                No degrees, no "sufficiently", no "adequately".
    OBSERVABLE: verifiable from the artifact plus declared inputs alone.
                No third-party reaction, no elapsed time, no reader
                judgment, no quality predicate.

    REJECT as non-binary or non-observable: comprehensive, clear,
    persuasive, polished, thorough, well-argued, appropriate, covers
    everything important, works well, reads cleanly.

    A rejected candidate is NOT discarded. Route verbatim:
      references a third party / world state / elapsed time → objective
      otherwise                                             → unclassified

    DERIVATION. If no stated condition passes, derive from the action:

      accepted when: [artifact type] exists and contains [stated
                     required elements]
                     ← derived from action; no acceptance criteria
                       stated

    If no required elements were stated, the derived condition is bare
    existence. This is correct. An honestly vacuous condition is
    preferable to an invented rigorous one.

    DO NOT STRENGTHEN. If the user's stated condition is weak but
    passes both tests, it enters the slot unchanged. Tightening a weak
    acceptance condition is quality maximization and is out of scope.

    Multiple conditions are conjunctive — all must hold. Disjunction
    appears only if the user stated it.
```

No new warning token. The `←` trace makes weakness visible, which keeps the taxonomy closed at two per D2.

